# Day 57 – Active Directory DNS, VirtualBox Lab Network & Windows 11 Client Preparation

## 🎯 Objective

Today's objective was to continue building the Active Directory home lab by connecting the Windows Server and Windows 11 virtual machines to the same VirtualBox lab network.

The Windows Server 2025 machine (`SERVER01`) already had Active Directory Domain Services installed from the previous lab. Today the focus was on:

* Configuring a dedicated VirtualBox NAT Network for the Active Directory lab.
* Moving SERVER01 from the original VirtualBox NAT network to the new lab network.
* Maintaining a stable IP address for SERVER01.
* Connecting the Windows 11 client to the same virtual network.
* Testing communication between the client and Domain Controller.
* Testing Active Directory DNS resolution.
* Understanding the difference between internal AD DNS and external Internet DNS.
* Troubleshooting external DNS resolution.

The main goal was to prepare `WIN11-CLIENT01` to become a domain-joined Windows workstation.

