# 🌐 DNS and Active Directory

One of the main lessons from today's lab was understanding the relationship between DNS and Active Directory.

Active Directory depends on DNS to allow clients to locate Domain Controllers and other Active Directory services.

The basic process is:

```text
WIN11-CLIENT01
       |
       | DNS query
       ↓
SERVER01 DNS
       |
       ↓
kpatel.test
       |
       ↓
Locate Domain Controller
       |
       ↓
Authentication
```

Therefore, the Windows client must use the internal Active Directory DNS server when communicating with the domain.

